# Performance baselines - KEEP IN VERSION CONTROL
# (Uncomment the line below to exclude from version control if needed)
# test/.performance_baselines.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ephemeral process / runtime junk
# ASREF-006 monorepo root hygiene + ASREF-G090 cutover readiness
# (packet tasks ASREF-012 / ASREF-013 / ASREF-014)
# ASREF-013 evidence cluster: ASREF-G020 core, ASREF-G030 control,
# ASREF-G040 task_sources, ASREF-G050 context/prompt — under agent_supervisor/
# ASREF-014 evidence cluster: ASREF-G060 analysis/proof, ASREF-G070 ops
# packages, ASREF-G080 todo_daemon/integrations — under agent_supervisor/
# Keep packaging and human surfaces at the root; do not version process state.
# Files already tracked before these rules landed may still appear in history
# until a follow-up `git rm --cached` (outside narrow cutover path scope):
#   git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch dashboard.out dashboard.pid err.txt
# Nested product trees are documented in docs/NESTED_PACKAGES.md — never treat
# them as process junk. Package goals ASREF-G020..ASREF-G080 live under
# ipfs_accelerate_py/agent_supervisor/, not as root ephemera.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/dashboard.out
/dashboard.pid
/err.txt
dashboard.out
dashboard.pid
err.txt
*.pid
nohup.out
/*.out
/core
core.*
*.core
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
*.swo
*.orig
*.rej

# Local/ephemeral data under data/ (WAL, ad-hoc DBs; keep intentional fixtures)
